@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="legal-page">
    <h1 class="legal-page__title">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>PersonalFinance ("we," "our," or "us") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our personal finance web application (the "Service").</p>
        <p>Please read this privacy policy carefully. By accessing or using our Service, you signify that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by this policy.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <h3>Account Information</h3>
        <p>When you create an account, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Email address</li>
            <li>Password (stored securely using hashing)</li>
            <li>Account creation date</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Financial Data You Enter</h3>
        <p>The core of our Service involves storing your personal financial information. We collect and store the data you voluntarily enter, including:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Budget categories and monthly budget plans</li>
            <li>Budget transactions and spending records</li>
            <li>Savings goals and targets</li>
            <li>Net worth parameters (assets, liabilities, income, expenses)</li>
            <li>User budget allocations and source preferences</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Google Drive Integration Data</h3>
        <p>If you connect your Google Drive account, we store:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Google Drive connection metadata</li>
            <li>Spreadsheet budget snapshots imported from your Google Sheets</li>
            <li>Spreadsheet transaction records</li>
            <li>Cached file information from Google Drive</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Community Content</h3>
        <p>If you participate in community features, we store:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Community stories and posts</li>
            <li>Comments on community posts</li>
            <li>Poll votes and likes</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Usage Data</h3>
        <p>We collect:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Saved articles</li>
            <li>Notification preferences and history</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>We use the following third-party services that may process your data:</p>

        <h3>Google Drive and Sheets API</h3>
        <p>If you connect your Google Drive, we use the Google Drive and Sheets API (googleapis.com) to read your spreadsheets. Your Google API key is used to authenticate these requests.</p>

        <h3>Google Fonts</h3>
        <p>We load fonts from Google Fonts (fonts.googleapis.com). This service may collect your IP address. See our <a asp-controller="Legal" asp-action="Cookies">Cookie Policy</a> for details.</p>

        <h3>unpkg CDN</h3>
        <p>We load the Lucide icon library from unpkg.com. This is a third-party content delivery network.</p>

        <h3>Brevo (Transactional Email)</h3>
        <p>We use Brevo to send transactional emails, such as account confirmation. Brevo processes your email address for delivery purposes.</p>

        <h3>Azure Hosting</h3>
        <p>Our application is hosted on Microsoft Azure. Your data is stored in Azure SQL Database. Azure may be located in the United States.</p>

        <h3>AI Chat Widget</h3>
        <p>Our Service includes an AI-powered chat feature. Interactions with this feature may be processed by a third-party AI provider. Do not share sensitive financial details in the chat.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Provide, maintain, and improve the Service</li>
            <li>Process your financial data and generate projections</li>
            <li>Send you transactional emails (account confirmation, etc.)</li>
            <li>Import data from your connected Google Drive spreadsheets</li>
            <li>Respond to your support requests</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Data Retention and Soft Deletion</h2>
        <p>When you delete data in our Service, we use a "soft delete" mechanism. This means the data is marked as deleted but remains in our database. This approach allows us to maintain data integrity and prevent accidental loss.</p>
        <p>If you request full data erasure (see below), we will process your request within 30 days. Soft-deleted data associated with your account will be permanently removed or anonymized during this period.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Your GDPR Rights</h2>
        <p>If you are located in the European Economic Area (EEA), you have the following rights under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR):</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Right of Access:</strong> Request a copy of your personal data</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Rectification:</strong> Correct inaccurate or incomplete data</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Erasure:</strong> Request deletion of your personal data ("right to be forgotten")</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Data Portability:</strong> Receive your data in a machine-readable format</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Object:</strong> Object to the processing of your personal data</li>
            <li><strong>Right to Restriction:</strong> Request restriction of processing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the details on our <a asp-controller="Legal" asp-action="Contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>International Data Transfers</h2>
        <p>Your data is stored on Microsoft Azure servers, which may be located in the United States. If you are outside the United States, your data will be transferred across borders. We rely on appropriate safeguards, such as Standard Contractual Clauses, to ensure your data remains protected.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Data Security</h2>
        <p>We use industry-standard security measures to protect your data, including encrypted connections (HTTPS), password hashing, and access controls. However, no method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>Our Service is not intended for children under 16. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under 16. If we learn we have collected data from a child under 16, we will delete it promptly.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of changes by posting the new policy on this page and updating the "Last updated" date. Your continued use of the Service after changes constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="legal-section">
        <h2>Contact Us</h2>
        <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us via our <a asp-controller="Legal" asp-action="Contact">Contact page</a>.</p>
    </section>
</div>
